A||||6||wwh0001|| Under Hood Light||||1||
Z||000000||wwh0001||12-23-1999||02:54 PM||||You know that little courtesy light under the hood ( front compartment)on the cowl behind the jack ? I have an 88 Formula and an 87 GT, both have the light and both did work. Now both don't. Not the bulb . All other lights work. It seems as though some things that go wrong with Fiero's are common so I thought I would  see if anyone has found the problem with this one. No power is getting to the bulb socket. Yet it is on the same circuit as the side marker lights; so why doesn't it work? Not the socket either since I did try replacing that. Must be a ground somewhere?<BR>Any help would be appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||12-23-1999||03:14 PM||||I  imagine that there is a switch somewhere that turns it on when you open the hood. I would look there.||||reg||1
Z||000002||wwh0001||12-23-1999||04:01 PM||||Thanks for the thoughts, but that light comes on whenever you turn your headlights/parking lights on. It doesn't have its own switch. I know that's not a great way to make a hood light but that's the way it works. It should get power whenever the lights are on. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodrv6||12-23-1999||05:06 PM||||The light in my 84 is wired through the same switch that lights the "Deck Ajar" light on the dash.  According to the wiring diagram in my 88 shop manual, the 88's are wired the same way.  The switch on my 84 corroded a little, and the light doesn't always come on unless I rotate the switch plunger a little. The light is wired so that it will not come on unless the parking lights are on, but there is a switch to turn it off when the hood (front trunk?) is closed.||||reg||4
Z||000004||wwh0001||12-24-1999||08:53 AM||||Never thought of the hood light being wired with the door ajar switch. I'll check it out. Thanks a lot. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Rodrv6||12-24-1999||12:34 PM||||That switch is mounted just to the left of the hood latch in front of the windshield.<BR>It is the "Deck Ajar" not the door switch.||||reg||1
Z||000006||wwh0001||12-24-1999||02:23 PM||||I checked it out. you were right. The deck ajar switch was stuck. I guess I never noticed the deck ajar light wasn't working when the hood was open. Anyway, both the ajar light and the hood light now work. Thanks.<p>[This message has been edited by wwh0001 (edited 12-24-1999).]||||reg||1
